WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.290
The school library keeps
every loan in a table:

2
00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.330
the title, the genre, and
how many days late it is.

3
00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:11.570
The librarian has one
question: which books are late?

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.930
Someone types a single line.

5
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.370
A moment later, just the
overdue titles appear.

6
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.470
No scrolling.

7
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.710
No ticking off books by hand.

8
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.430
So how can one line of SQL
find every overdue book?

9
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:29.910
In this mission, you'll learn
SQL, Structured Query Language.

10
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:32.750
It's used to search
for data in a database.

11
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:35.910
You'll start by asking for just
the fields you want to see,

12
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.930
such as each book's title.

13
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:42.080
Your mission: work out what
that one blurred line must say.
